- **Concepts:** LB, cache, Redis, SQL/NoSQL, indexing, horizontal/vertical scaling, CAP, replication, sharding, queues, CDN, API gateway, rate limiter, microservices, async/event-driven, consistency models, pagination, WebSockets, auth, monitoring.  
- **Diagrams:** Single diagrams to sketch: e.g. load balancer with servers; client–queue–worker; gateway–services; sharded DB; pub/sub model; CDN architecture.  
- **Algorithms:** Token bucket & sliding window for rate limit; mention LRU for cache eviction.  
- **Numbers:** Common volumes: e.g. ~100k ops/s for Redis【64†L190-L198】, typical sizes (single machine ~256 TB limit), etc. (Even saying “fast SSDs can handle millions IOPS” can sound savvy).  
- **Failures:** What happens if each component fails (servers crash, DB down, cache down, network partition). Have an answer ready.  
- **Phrases:** E.g. “This prevents a single point of failure,” “We should consider eventual consistency if needed,” “Let’s decouple with a queue,” etc.  

